## Agentic pipeline

This repo uses the `agentic` plugin (https://github.com/christophe77/agentic-delivery-pipeline).
Configuration: `.agentic/pipeline.yml`.

### Cycle
1. `/agentic:epic <need>`: epic in Monday (human approval)
2. `/agentic:tickets <epic id>`: tickets as vertical slices (human approval)
3. `/agentic:implement <ticket id>`: branch, code, tests, PR
4. `/agentic:review <PR>`: local review; CI runs a new review on every push
5. Merge: **human**
6. Automatic staging deployment, then `/agentic:qa` (CI)
7. `/agentic:release prepare`: production deployment (GitHub approval required)
8. `/agentic:release close`: Monday tickets moved to Done

### Conventions
- Branches: `{type}/{item_id}-{slug}` (e.g. `feat/1234567890-export-csv`)
- Conventional commits, with a `Monday: #<item_id>` footer
- One PR = one ticket
- Definition of done: acceptance criteria tested, lint/tests/build green, review with no blocker, QA passed on staging

